<body>

<div class="title-page">
  <h1>ACCBOT WEB SYSTEM</h1>
  <h2>Database Design & Relational Reference Document</h2>
  <br><br><br>
  <p><strong>Prepared For:</strong> Database Administrators & System Developers</p>
  <p><strong>Subject:</strong> PostgreSQL Schema, Triggers, RLS Policies, and Proposed Ledger Schema</p>
  <p><strong>Database Platform:</strong> PostgreSQL (hosted on Supabase Cloud)</p>
  <p><strong>Version:</strong> 1.0 (Production Blueprint)</p>
  <p><strong>Date:</strong> July 4, 2026</p>
</div>

<h1 class="first">1. Database Overview & Security</h1>
<p>The Accbot database structure uses PostgreSQL hosted on Supabase. To ensure secure multi-tenant structures and protect private data, the system uses Row Level Security (RLS) on all tables. Database tables are accessible through postgrest auto-generated REST APIs or Next.js Server Actions. Access is controlled by Postgres RLS policy rules based on the user's role (<span class="highlight">super_admin</span>, <span class="highlight">admin</span>, <span class="highlight">user</span>).</p>

<h2>Database Security Features</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Row Level Security (RLS):</strong> Every query is verified against user authentication contexts (<span class="highlight">auth.uid()</span>) to prevent users from accessing other accounts' records.</li>
  <li><strong>Definer Functions:</strong> Administrative functions run under a SECURITY DEFINER context, allowing limited database tasks to bypass standard user RLS restrictions.</li>
  <li><strong>Cascade Actions:</strong> Deleting an auth user automatically deletes the corresponding profile and related activity logs.</li>
</ul>

<h1>2. Entity Relationship Diagram (ERD - Conceptual)</h1>
<p>The schema focuses on user profiles as the central entity. The diagram below illustrates the relationships between the database tables:</p>

<div class="code-block">
 +-----------------+                +-----------------+
 |   auth.users    |                |  testimonials   |
 +-----------------+                +-----------------+
        || 1:1                             ||
        || (Trigger)                       || (Public read if active)
        v                                  v
 +-----------------+                +-----------------+
 | public.profiles | <=== 1:N ====> |   blog_posts    |
 +-----------------+                +-----------------+
   ||           ||                     (author_id)
   || 1:N       || 1:N
   v            v
 +-----------------+  +-----------------+  +-----------------+
 |  activity_logs  |  |contact_messages |  |    services     |
 +-----------------+  +-----------------+  +-----------------+
                      (Public insert)      (Public read if active)
</div>

<h1>3. Database Tables Reference (Existing Schema)</h1>

<h3>Table 1: public.profiles</h3>
<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Stores user profiles and roles. Syncs with <span class="highlight">auth.users</span> via trigger.</p>
<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Column Name</th>
      <th>Data Type</th>
      <th>Constraints</th>
      <th>Default Value</th>
      <th>Description</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td>id</td>
      <td>uuid</td>
      <td>PRIMARY KEY, REFERENCES auth.users ON DELETE CASCADE</td>
      <td>None</td>
      <td>Links directly to auth.users.id.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>full_name</td>
      <td>text</td>
      <td>NOT NULL</td>
      <td>None</td>
      <td>User's display name.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>email</td>
      <td>text</td>
      <td>NOT NULL, UNIQUE</td>
      <td>None</td>
      <td>User's email. Used for identity verification.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>phone</td>
      <td>text</td>
      <td>Nullable</td>
      <td>None</td>
      <td>User's phone number.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>avatar_url</td>
      <td>text</td>
      <td>Nullable</td>
      <td>None</td>
      <td>Link to the profile avatar image.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>role</td>
      <td>text</td>
      <td>NOT NULL, CHECK (role IN ('super_admin', 'admin', 'user'))</td>
      <td>'user'</td>
      <td>System permission tier.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>created_at</td>
      <td>timestamp with time zone</td>
      <td>NOT NULL</td>
      <td>timezone('utc'::text, now())</td>
      <td>Creation timestamp.</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td>updated_at</td>
      <td>timestamp with time zone</td>
      <td>NOT NULL</td>
      <td>timezone('utc'::text, now())</td>
      <td>Modification timestamp.</td>
    </tr>
  </tbody>
</table>

